# What `docker build .` must not send to the daemon.
#
# Both Dockerfiles use `COPY . .` with the workspace root as context, and the
# hub's own header documents a local build as a supported flow. Without this
# file that flow sends the whole working directory — a Rust `target/` reaches
# hundreds of gigabytes on a machine that has run the test suite a few times,
# and the transfer never finishes. CI never noticed because a fresh checkout
# has no target/.
#
# The builder stage runs `cargo build` itself, so nothing here is needed inside
# the image. Keeping it out also stops a host-built artifact from being mistaken
# for a fresh one.

# Every cargo --target-dir, not just the default one: `target-pg17` (the
# second PostgreSQL major the pgupgrade stage needs) and `target-test` are
# each ~10GB on this machine, and `target-pg*` alone missed the second.
target*/
**/node_modules/

# Hub runtime state, if someone has run a hub from the repo root.
hub_identity.json
hub.search/
*.wavvon-backup
pgdata/

.git/
.github/
*.log

# Local compose overrides and env files — never baked into an image.
.env
.env.*
docker-compose.dev.yml

# The web client source CI checks out at this path is the one exception: the
# web-builder stage copies `web-client-src*` on purpose, so it must NOT be
# ignored. Listed here so nobody adds it by reflex.
!web-client-src/
